  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Decision\\n\\n**Record A applies: the observation cursor is global — one position shared by all readers of the store.**\\n\\n## How I got there\\n\\n**1. The two records are a genuine same-scope conflict, not locally self-resolving.**\\n`docs/engineering/09-observation-contract-a.md` and `-b.md` are structurally identical: same \\\"normative, current scope\\\" status, same \\\"Version scope: current pinned line\\\", no dates, no revision ids, no cross-references. Neither is reachable from `docs/engineering/README.md`'s archive index (their `09-` number collides with the indexed `09-adaptive-allocation-spec.md`), and repo-wide search finds no other document that references or supersedes either one. So the records can't be ranked against each other by their own text.\\n\\n**2. The workspace fixes the version scope by its pin.**\\nThis workspace is the Palimpsest DSH plugin, and the integration in question is its consumption of Ordarium. The pin actually in force is **`ordarium-v1.3.1`**, consistently across three layers:\\n\\n- `package.json` dependencies (core / host-kit / ledger-sqlite / testing),\\n- `pnpm-workspace.yaml` `overrides` (the load-bearing pnpm 11 location per `07-ordarium-alignment.md`",
